  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2f4848e7e46289243b311920bdbdddf0, type: 3}
  m_Name: Cryptography
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  playerLines:
  - I always wondered how my messages get encrypted so other can't understand them
  - I mean I barely understand how it works myself
  - Wow I didn't realize how important it was
  - <i>hmm...</i>
  - <i>Understanding what your opponent is doing seems to be vital to winning battles</i>
  - <i>Deciphering how things work and the opponent's strategy for myself is something
    I may need to consider</i>
  NPCLines:
  - Cryptography is one of the most important studies for everyday life
  - It keeps us safe from attackers out to steal our data
  - One of the simplest encryption techniques is the Ceasar cipher
  - One of the simplest and most well-known encryption techniques is the Caesar cipher
  - Named and used by Julius Caesar in the 1st century BCE, it is a simple substitution
    cipher
  - Letters are replaced by shifting the alphabet across
  - Another famous encryption system was the Enigma machine
  - The importance of cracking this system is one of the biggest reasons computer
    science exists these days
  - 'The primitive computer: <i>bombe</i> that Alan Turing designed in Bletchley
    Park was one of the deciding factors of WW2'
  speakTurnPlayer: 010100000000000001000000010101
